p's current default shortcut table covers the direct tool keys used for selection, drawing, modeling, and camera control. These entries apply to the Windows and Mac desktop defaults.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable SketchUp sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=sketchup)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/slack","title":"<mark>Slack</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Slack's shortcut map spans the desktop shell, conversations, workspaces, tabs, messages, huddles, and canvas editing. This page keeps those contexts together and calls out desktop-only or keyboard-layout-sensitive bindings.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Slack sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=slack)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/smartsheet","title":"<mark>Smartsheet</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Smartsheet's official keyboard shortcut table covers sheet editing, search, hierarchy, formatting, row selection, date entry, and dashboard focus. Windows and Mac mappings are shown separately where they differ.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Smartsheet sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=smartsheet)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/solidworks","title":"<mark>SOLIDWORKS</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"SOLIDWORKS Design Help publishes selected Windows shortcuts for assemblies, copying, display, selection, sketching, and the shortcut bar. The record focuses on stable key commands rather than mouse gestures.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable SOLIDWORKS sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=solidworks)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/spark-mail","title":"<mark>Spark Mail</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Spark Mail's desktop shortcut reference groups email triage, navigation, composing, formatting, calendar, and team actions. This record uses the published Mac and Windows desktop presets.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Spark Mail sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=spark-mail)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/spotify","title":"<mark>Spotify</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Spotify's current desktop support page lists shortcuts for search, playback, library navigation, sidebars, and queue actions. The table below keeps its Mac and Windows differences explicit.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Spotify sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=spotify)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/squarespace","title":"<mark>Squarespace</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Squarespace's official guide covers site navigation, Fluid Engine block editing, text formatting, and Acuity actions. These entries describe the current Mac and Windows editing shortcuts.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Squarespace sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=squarespace)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/sublime-text","title":"<mark>Sublime Text</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Sublime Text's current community documentation publishes separate Windows/Linux and macOS tables for editing, navigation, builds, search, tabs, folding, and bookmarks.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Sublime Text sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=sublime-text)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/superhuman","title":"<mark>Superhuman</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Superhuman's official shortcut guide covers inbox triage, search, composing, formatting, navigation, and tabs. This reference pairs the desktop modifier differences while keeping single-key actions readable.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Superhuman sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=superhuman)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/tableau","title":"<mark>Tableau</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Tableau's official shortcut reference covers Desktop workbooks, authoring, data, dashboards, marks, and worksheet navigation. This curated set keeps the most-used Windows and Mac defaults together.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Tableau sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=tableau)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/tableplus","title":"<mark>TablePlus</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"TablePlus's official shortcut documentation covers connections, workspaces, SQL editing, panes, query execution, and table data. Windows entries use the documented Control replacement for Command.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable TablePlus sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=tableplus)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/tally-forms","title":"<mark>Tally Forms</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Tally's official keyboard shortcut guide covers form editing, block movement, formatting, command menus, and Markdown-style input. The shared web shortcuts are paired across Windows, macOS, and Linux.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Tally Forms sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=tally-forms)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/telegram","title":"<mark>Telegram</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Telegram Desktop publishes its default shortcut actions in the open-source desktop implementation and exposes them in Chat Settings. This reference focuses on chat, folder, window, and message navigation.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Telegram sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=telegram)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/things-3","title":"<mark>Things 3</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Things 3's official Mac shortcut reference covers task creation, scheduling, navigation, Markdown styling, search, and list organization. iPad and iPhone shortcuts are outside this Mac record.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Things 3 sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=things-3)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/tmux","title":"<mark>tmux</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"tmux's default prefix map controls sessions, windows, panes, copy mode, and terminal layout without leaving a shell. The entries use tmux's default Ctrl-B prefix and preserve the distinction between a prefix chord and the command key that follows it.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable tmux sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=tmux)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/todoist","title":"<mark>Todoist</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Todoist's current reference covers general app navigation, quick add, global desktop controls, task editing, projects, sorting, upcoming view, calendar layout, and multi-window workflows. This map keeps web and desktop commands together while showing platform-specific bindings explicitly.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Todoist sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=todoist)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/typora","title":"<mark>Typora</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Typora's official shortcut table covers file operations, Markdown editing, headings, lists, formatting, search, views, and document navigation. The Windows and Linux defaults are paired, while macOS command and option variants stay explicit.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Typora sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=typora)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/ulysses","title":"<mark>Ulysses</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Ulysses' official Mac reference covers sheets and groups, library navigation, search, editor markup, tables, previews, appearance, and export. The app's iPad and iPhone hardware-keyboard maps are separate, so this record stays Mac-only.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Ulysses sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=ulysses)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/vim","title":"<mark>Vim</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Vim is a language of motions, operators, and modes rather than a list of isolated hotkeys. This reference covers the normal, insert, visual, search, window, and command-line paths that make the official quick reference useful at the keyboard.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Vim sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=vim)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/visual-studio","title":"<mark>Visual Studio</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Visual Studio's General profile includes distinct defaults for building, debugging, editing, files, projects, refactoring, views, and document windows. This Windows reference keeps the common commands and their context notes readable instead of flattening every context-specific command into one list.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Visual Studio sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=visual-studio)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/vmware-workstation","title":"<mark>VMware Workstation</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"VMware Workstation's default hot-key combinations release input, control full-screen guests, switch virtual machines, and manage Unity mode. This reference covers the host shortcuts documented for Workstation Pro on Windows and Linux.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable VMware Workstation sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=vmware-workstation)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/vscode","title":"<mark>Visual Studio Code</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"VS Code's default shortcuts cover the whole coding loop: edit and navigate code, search and refactor, manage files and panels, run tasks, debug, and use the built-in chat tools. This reference follows Microsoft's current common default list for a standard US keyboard layout.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Visual Studio Code sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=vscode)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/warp","title":"<mark>Warp</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Warp's official shortcut reference covers panes, blocks, terminal input, command search, tabs, navigation, and font controls across macOS, Windows, and Linux. The map preserves Warp's platform-specific defaults, including Emacs-style input bindings shared by the terminal editor.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Warp sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=warp)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/webflow","title":"<mark>Webflow</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Webflow's current designer reference covers canvas editing, breakpoints, panels, classes, interactions, element movement, and publishing. Webflow documents Command and Option on Mac with Control and Alt equivalents on Windows, which this map keeps explicit.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Webflow sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=webflow)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/webstorm","title":"<mark>WebStorm</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"WebStorm's default keymap covers search, code completion, editing, navigation, refactoring, files, tabs, debugging, and version control. The reference uses the standard Windows/Linux and macOS keymaps and keeps two-stroke commands labeled as sequences.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable WebStorm sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=webstorm)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/whimsical","title":"<mark>Whimsical</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Whimsical publishes separate current shortcut tables for its Windows and Mac apps. This reference covers workspace navigation, boards, diagrams, mind maps, and notes.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Whimsical sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=whimsical)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/windows-file-explorer","title":"<mark>Windows File Explorer</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Microsoft publishes a dedicated File Explorer section in its current Windows keyboard shortcut reference. This map covers navigation, tabs, search, panes, and file actions.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Windows File Explorer sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=windows-file-explorer)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/windows-snipping-tool","title":"<mark>Windows Snipping Tool</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Microsoft documents shortcuts for opening the Snipping Tool capture overlays and for working inside the Snipping Tool editor.","content_markdown":"<!-- section:print -->\n## Print the shortcuts you use\n\n[Make a printable Windows Snipping Tool sheet](/shortcuts-cheatsheet-generator?apps=windows-snipping-tool)"},{"slug":"keyboard-shortcuts/windows-terminal","title":"<mark>Windows Terminal</mark> keyboard shortcuts","intro_markdown":"Windows Terminal is a workspace for several shells, so its important keys manage the container around the prompt. Open tabs, split panes, search scrollback, copy and paste, zoom, and reach